OL,3,GNEWSAThe British island where red
OL,4,Asquirrels are thriving
OL,5,
OL,6,FWith growing concerns that red
OL,7,Fsquirrels could soon become extinct in
OL,8,FEngland, one Channel Island is a corner
OL,9,Fof the British Isles where they
OL,10,Fmaintain a stronghold.
OL,12,FJersey is home to a thriving red
OL,13,Fsquirrel population, thanks to the
OL,14,Fcomplete absence of grey squirrels,
OL,15,Fwhich carry a virus deadly to their red
OL,16,Fcousins.
OL,18,FRed squirrels are endangered in the UK,
OL,19,Fwith about 120,000 to 160,000 left in
OL,20,Fthe wild and various projects are
OL,21,Faiming to boost those numbers.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
